course: dictionary
lesson: 15580
title: Swimwear and words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Swimwear is a word for clothes you wear for swimming. It is a general word, so it covers many kinds of swimming clothes: swimsuits, swimming trunks, bikinis and rash vests. «Please bring your swimwear, a towel and goggles to swimming lessons.» The sentence tells you that swimwear is something you bring to the pool, so it must be clothes for the water.
explain: Swimwear is a group word, like clothing. You do not say «a swimwear». You say «the swimwear section» or «new swimwear for the holiday». Swimwear is uncountable, so you do not add an s to it.
explain: Context helps you again. «The shop has a big swimwear section near the door.» A section is one part of a shop where similar things are sold, so swimwear is a kind of clothing for sale. To check, swap in your own meaning: «The shop has a big swimming clothes section near the door.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Some people use different words for swimwear. You might hear «swimsuit» or «swimming costume». In Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, people may say «togs» or «cozzie», and in parts of Australia they say «bathers». When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, and check a dictionary if you are still not sure.
fact: Swimwear means clothing for swimming.
fact: Swimsuits, swimming trunks, bikinis and rash vests are all kinds of swimwear.
fact: Swimwear is uncountable, so you do not add an s to it.
fact: Bright swimwear is easier for lifeguards to see in the water.
fact: «Togs» and «cozzie» are words for swimwear in Australia, New Zealand and Ireland.
exercise: «Please bring your swimwear, a towel and goggles.» What is swimwear? | A towel for drying | A pair of trainers | *Clothing for swimming | A pair of goggles
exercise: «The swimwear section is on the second floor.» Where would you find swimwear? | At the bus stop | Under the sea | *In a shop | In a park
exercise: Which of these is a kind of swimwear? | *A rash vest | A school jumper | Wellington boots | A sunhat
test: Lifeguards can spot bright swimwear easily in the water. Why is bright swimwear useful? | It is cheaper to buy | It keeps the swimmer warm in winter | It makes the swimmer faster | *It is easier for lifeguards to see
test: In Australia someone says, «Grab your togs, we are going to the beach.» What does togs mean? | *Swimwear | Sun cream | Towels | Sandals
exam: Which sentence uses swimwear correctly? | Mia bought a swimwear for the summer | Mia bought swimwears for the summer | *Mia bought new swimwear for the summer | Mia bought three swimwears for the summer
